kosha car-motion

  -- the energy conversion chain of a car.
  -- chemical bonds (fuel) → heat (combustion) → mechanical rotation (engine)
  -- → linear KE (tyre friction) → heat (brake friction) → rest.
  --
  -- driving: tyre static friction is the force that moves the car forward.
  --   engine torque → wheel rotation → contact patch pushes backward on road
  --   → Newton 3: road pushes forward on car = driving force.
  --   no friction = no motion. a car on ice cannot accelerate.
  --
  -- braking: brake pad kinetic friction converts KE → heat.
  --   Q = ½mv² (all KE) if braking to rest.
  --   ABS keeps friction static (higher μ) → shorter stopping distance.
  --
  -- janya: fuel (hydrocarbon), mass, velocity, friction-coefficient.
  -- phala: velocity-change (acceleration or deceleration), heat.

  "common-sense-varga-vishesa"
